================================================================================
CHANGES MADE TO NVIDIA SOURCE (Apache-2.0 section 4b)
================================================================================

solref/fwd.py:

  1. Replaced the two upstream imports

         from sol_attn.interface import _validate
         from sol_attn.preprocess  import prepare

     with a local relative import of `prepare`, plus a local copy of
     `_validate`. Upstream `sol_attn/interface.py` imports `cuda.bindings.driver`
     and `cutlass.cute` at module scope; those are CUTLASS-DSL dependencies
     required only by the hand-written SM90/SM100 CuTe kernels, not by the
     Triton reference kernel. Importing it would fail on installs that do not
     carry the CUTLASS DSL.

  2. REMOVED THE GPU ARCHITECTURE GATE from the local copy of `_validate`:

         arch = torch.cuda.get_device_capability(q.device)
         if arch not in ((9, 0), (10, 0)):
             raise RuntimeError("Sol-Attn supports H100 (SM90) and B200 (SM100)")

     Rationale: that check guards `interface.py`'s dispatcher, which selects
     between hand-written CuTe kernels that exist only for SM90 and SM100. The
     Triton kernel in this file is JIT-compiled by Triton for whatever
     architecture it is given and has no such dependency. Every other upstream
     validation (rank, shape, head_dim == 128, bfloat16, device, contiguity,
     kv_splits, thresh_type, route-group count) is retained verbatim.

     THIS IS AN UNSANCTIONED CHANGE. NVIDIA does not claim support for, and has
     not validated, Sol-Attn on architectures outside SM90/SM100. Numerical
     behaviour and performance on other architectures are the responsibility of
     this repository, not NVIDIA's. See README "Scope and caveats".

  No other lines of upstream source were altered. The Triton kernel `_forward`,
  its autotune configuration, and the `sol_attn()` launch path are untouched.

